claim.claim-text:
providing, as inputs, an alternative amino-acid sequence comprising a variant amino acid, a reference amino-acid, and at least a position frequency matrix to a trained variant pathogenicity prediction model comprising parameters that have been tuned based on supplemental training example amino-acid sequence pairs;
determining pathogenicity predictions for the variant amino acid utilizing an ensemble of networks of the trained variant pathogenicity prediction model; and
generating, based on the pathogenicity predictions for the variant amino acid, a pathogenicity prediction indicating a likelihood that the variant amino acid is benign or pathogenic.

a first position frequency matrix based on amino acids from an order of organisms;
a second position frequency matrix based on amino acids from a class of organisms; or
a third position frequency matrix based on amino acids from a subphylum of organisms.
